      "glyphModes": {
        "source": "clementina-rom src/kernel/editor.s edit_echo; the mode is EDIT_MODE",
        "count": 3,
        "step": 96,
        "firstKey": 32,
        "lastKey": 126,
        "notes": [
          "In glyph mode m the screen editor turns a typed character code k from firstKey to lastKey into tile (k + m * step) mod 256 and draws it as a glyph. Other codes keep their usual meaning.",
          "ESC M steps the mode 0, 1, 2, 0; ESC SPACE returns to mode 0 and resets the pen. The cursor shows the mode (kernelTiles).",
          "Mode 0 types $20-$7E, mode 1 $80-$DE and mode 2 $E0-$FF and $00-$3E. No key types $7F or $DF; a program draws any tile with KERN_CHROUT_GLYPH."
        ]
      }
